   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The B1 level begins",
     "texto": [
      "Up to here you've learned to get by in everyday life. In B1 you'll **tell, explain and give reasons**: why you do something, what happened, what plans you have.",
      "The sentences get a little longer, but the trick is always the same: in Vietnamese ideas are linked with **pairs of words**. Learn the pair and you'll have the sentence.",
      "In each reading, first try to grasp the general idea and answer the questions with the translation hidden; then show it to check which clues helped you."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Cause and effect: vì… nên…",
     "texto": [
      "To say «because… / as…, (so)…» you use the pair **vì… nên…**: first the cause, then the consequence. «**Vì** trời mưa **nên** tôi ở nhà» = Because it's raining, I'm staying at home.",
      "In English it's enough to say «as» or «so». In Vietnamese it's very normal to say **both**: vì (because) + nên (so).",
      "There are other common ways to present causes: **do** = due to (appears a lot in explanations and formal texts, but isn't limited to them); **nhờ** usually presents a favourable cause (thanks to), and **tại** usually presents an unfavourable cause or a complaint (because of). The nuance depends on the context. «**Nhờ** anh giúp **nên** tôi làm xong» = Thanks to your help I finished. «**Tại** kẹt xe **nên** tôi đến muộn» = Because of the traffic jam I arrived late."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
